<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Java</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Javanese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Java is a densely populated island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> and an important rival or part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> sphere. It later became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonial economy, with its headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a>, and was the target of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> expedition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/java.jpg" alt="Java" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sadalmelik · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Java_Topography.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
